  "blocks": {
    "\"It made fourteen tool calls inside that turn — each one is a separate model provider request. Latency stacks up before the agent finally yields back to you.\"": "“它在那个轮次中进行了 14 次<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/tool-call\">工具调用</a>——每次都是独立的模型提供商请求。延迟会不断累积，直到智能体最终把控制权交还给你。”",
    "\"One turn took two minutes?\"": "“一个轮次用了两分钟？”",
    "One user message plus everything the agent does in response, up until it yields back to the user. Contains one or more model provider requests — many, if the agent calls tools. A clarifying question closes the turn; your reply opens the next one. The hierarchy is session > Turn > Model provider request.": "一个轮次包括一条用户消息，以及<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/agent\">智能体</a>为响应它所做的一切，直到智能体把控制权交还给用户。一个轮次包含一次或多次<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/model-provider-request\">模型提供商请求</a>；如果智能体调用<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/tool\">工具</a>，请求数量可能很多。智能体提出澄清问题时，当前轮次结束；你的回复会开启下一轮。层级关系是：<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/session\">会话</a> > 轮次 > 模型提供商请求。",
    "The turn is also the natural unit for steering. Everything inside a turn happens without you; the gaps between turns are where you redirect. Most harnesses soften this: you can interrupt mid-turn to stop the agent and redirect it, or type a message while it works, which gets read once the turn completes. If you find yourself repeatedly unhappy with where turns end up, the fix is usually to ask for smaller ones — a plan first, one step at a time — trading autonomy for more frequent gaps to steer in.": "轮次也是引导智能体的自然单位。轮次内部发生的一切都没有你的参与；轮次之间的空隙才是你纠正方向的位置。大多数<a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/harness\">运行框架</a>会缓解这一限制：可以在轮次中途打断智能体并重新引导，也可以在它工作时输入消息，等轮次结束后再读取。如果你反复对轮次最终走向不满意，通常应要求更小的轮次——先给计划、每次只做一步——用部分自主性换取更频繁的引导机会。",
    "Usage:": "<em>用法：</em>",
    "What makes the turn worth naming is that its length is the agent's decision, not yours. You hand over one message; the agent decides how many tool calls to chain before yielding. A turn can be a one-sentence answer or twenty minutes of reading, editing, and running tests. That's the same property from two angles: long turns are what make AFK work possible, and long turns are also where things go wrong unsupervised — by the time the agent yields, it may have drifted a long way from what you meant.": "之所以需要单独命名“轮次”，是因为其长度由智能体决定，而不是由你决定。你交出一条消息，智能体自行决定在返回控制权前串联多少次工具调用。一个轮次可以只包含一句回答，也可以持续 20 分钟，期间不断读取、编辑和运行测试。同一性质有两个侧面：长轮次让 <a href=\"/ai-coding-dictionary/afk\">AFK</a> 工作成为可能；无人监督时，问题也最容易在长轮次中发生——等智能体终于返回时，它可能已经远远偏离你的本意。"
  },
